        "description": "<div id=\"remove_no_follow\">\n\t\t<div class=\"grid grid--cols-10@md grid--cols-8@lg article-column\">\n\t\t\t\t\t  <div class=\"col-12 col-10@md col-6@lg col-start-3@lg\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"article-column__content\">\n<section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Nowadays, most modern laptops don\u2019t have an Ethernet port. It\u2019s a fairly large port, and with laptops getting thinner and thinner, there simply isn\u2019t enough room for one. However, if you still wish to enjoy the benefits of a fast and stable LAN connection, you can always use an adapter or a docking station.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Even if you can set up a LAN connection with an adapter, you should check whether you\u2019re actually achieving the optimal data rate. For a gigabit adapter with 1000 Mbit/s, this should be around 950 Mbit/s. If this isn\u2019t the case, there are several steps you can take to resolve the issue.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"upd",
